# CommercializationPlans

**Status:** Draft — founder review required
**Phase:** 5 — Application System

## Purpose

Holds reusable narrative content around how funded work translates into
real business outcomes — the "what happens after the grant" story that
many funders (especially innovation/economic-development programs) require
and that `GrantWriter-Agent` draws from rather than re-writing from
scratch each time.

## What Lives Here

- **Growth/scaling narrative** — how grant-funded work fits into the
  business's broader growth trajectory
- **Sustainability plan language** — what continues after the grant period
  ends (ties directly to `ProposalTemplates.md` section 9)
- **Prior commercialization outcomes** — if a past grant or investment led
  to a real, describable business result, that becomes reusable proof
  points for future applications
- **Market/impact framing** — how the work benefits customers, the local
  economy (relevant for BHI's Michiana service area), or the trade more
  broadly, depending on funder type

## Notes

- This file should be populated with real, founder-confirmed language, not
  invented outcomes — per the Truth Standard in `GOVERNANCE.md`,
  overstating commercialization results is exactly the kind of fabrication
  that scores worse than an honest "this is a new initiative with no track
  record yet"
- Foundation-category applications (see `FoundationGrants.md`) tend to lean
  most heavily on this file, since mission/impact framing matters more
  there than in Federal/State categories

